      },
      "material_ids": [
        "docs/apply.md:1:100",
        "replication.go:202:298",
        "transport.go:1:74",
        "commitment.go:1:104",
        "api.go:803:907",
        "raft.go:1440:1584",
        "fsm.go:1:180"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "Unsuccessful Apply outcomes and user-initiated snapshot replacement are excluded by the goal."
          ],
          "target_id": "G_apply",
          "aspect": "applicability",
          "status": "no_issue_found",
          "source_ids": [
            "docs/apply.md:1:100",
            "api.go:803:907",
            "fsm.go:1:180",
            "commitment.go:1:104"
          ],
          "explanation": "The goal has an attributed contractual basis: the Apply documentation requires durable quorum storage before FSM application, and the FSM interface requires majority commitment before Apply. The API's uncertainty after ErrLeadershipLost does not contradict a goal restricted to successful completion. This provisionally supports the goal's applicability to ordinary Apply; it does not establish that any particular storage backend, membership history or completion path satisfies it.",
          "alternatives": "BatchingFSM changes the application mechanism while retaining a commitment prerequisite. Snapshot catch-up may supply prefix support without retaining every original log entry.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "Correct arithmetic over reported indexes can coexist with reports that do not represent durable matching prefixes, or with incorrect downstream completion. Thus O_commit alone cannot establish this goal.",
          "limitations": [
            "The applicable configuration-transition and persistence contracts remain unresolved.",
            "The complete leader commitment-to-FSM completion path is not supplied."
          ]
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "Report truth, configuration-change legality, startIndex initialization and end-to-end Apply completion are excluded."
          ],
          "target_id": "O_commit",
          "aspect": "applicability",
          "status": "no_issue_found",
          "source_ids": [
            "commitment.go:1:104",
            "docs/apply.md:1:100"
          ],
          "explanation": "The commitment component's comments assign it monotonically increasing commitment from voter progress and identify startIndex as the threshold required before commitment. These attributed responsibilities support the local obligation independently of the observed sorting implementation. The obligation correctly constrains advances under the current voter map and confines report monotonicity to match calls.",
          "alternatives": "An unchanged commitIndex may retain historically established commitment after voter-map replacement without obtaining fresh support from the replacement map.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "A replacement map with lower reported indexes does not itself violate this obligation when commitIndex remains unchanged. A match call that decreased its tracked value, or a new advance below startIndex, would contradict the selected local responsibility.",
          "limitations": [
            "The supplied material does not establish that the caller's startIndex identifies the first entry of the leader's term."
          ]
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "This is a component obligation over reported values, not a sufficient decomposition of G_apply.",
            "Notification delivery and downstream consumption are outside the arithmetic focus."
          ],
          "target_id": "O_commit",
          "aspect": "decomposition",
          "status": "no_issue_found",
          "source_ids": [
            "commitment.go:1:104",
            "docs/apply.md:1:100"
          ],
          "explanation": "Initialization, membership filtering, increasing report admission, voter-map replacement and guarded advancement cover the selected component transitions. A strict majority must be evaluated against the map at the advancing operation. Monotonic commitIndex is distinct from per-voter progress: setConfiguration preserves surviving IDs but forgets removed IDs, so later reintroduction can initialize an ID to zero. The obligation's restriction to match reports avoids requiring permanent per-ID history.",
          "alternatives": "The majority threshold could be computed by counting supporting voters rather than sorting. Either mechanism must satisfy the same local responsibility. Historical commitment can survive membership replacement without a new advance.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "All clauses can hold while the broader goal fails because reports are unsound, the voter configuration is inappropriate, startIndex is misinitialized, or the consumer applies the wrong entry. These dependencies remain outside the selected obligation.",
          "limitations": [
            "No formal checker, execution or ordered reachability evidence was supplied."
          ]
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "Caller validation and initialization semantics are outside this binding's direct behavior."
          ],
          "target_id": "B_newCommitment",
          "aspect": "decomposition",
          "status": "no_issue_found",
          "source_ids": [
            "commitment.go:1:104"
          ],
          "explanation": "The declaration anchor at line 35 and behavior range 35–48 identify newCommitment. It selects Voter IDs, initializes their indexes and commitIndex to zero, and retains the supplied startIndex. The association to O_commit and U_commit's direct establishment use accurately describe that behavior.",
          "alternatives": "Validation could occur in callers; this constructor does not establish it. Distinct configuration entries with the same ServerID map to one key.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "An incorrect supplied startIndex would not invalidate this location or initialization mapping, but could invalidate an attempted interpretation of the threshold as current-term support.",
          "limitations": []
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "The binding does not establish the identity, agreement or persistence represented by a report."
          ],
          "target_id": "B_match",
          "aspect": "decomposition",
          "status": "no_issue_found",
          "source_ids": [
            "commitment.go:1:104"
          ],
          "explanation": "The declaration anchor at line 77 and behavior range 77–84 identify match. Under the mutex it admits only reports for tracked IDs whose indexes exceed stored progress, then invokes recalculate. This supports the O_commit association and the unit's direct use for report admission.",
          "alternatives": "Equal, stale and nonvoter reports are ignored. Membership replacement has separate progress-retention semantics and is not a match report.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "A numerically increasing but false report can pass this filter. The binding therefore supports local admission checks without establishing O_replication_support.",
          "limitations": []
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "Legal membership sequencing is a caller responsibility outside this binding."
          ],
          "target_id": "B_setConfiguration",
          "aspect": "decomposition",
          "status": "no_issue_found",
          "source_ids": [
            "commitment.go:1:104"
          ],
          "explanation": "The declaration anchor at line 53 and behavior range 53–64 identify setConfiguration. The implementation rebuilds the voter map under lock, copies values for IDs present in the immediately preceding map, defaults other values to zero and recalculates. Its association and direct unit use accurately capture a transition affecting commitment arithmetic.",
          "alternatives": "The component could have retained progress for removed IDs, but this implementation does not. Existing commitment can remain unchanged when the new map has less reported support.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "After an ID is removed, readding it initializes its stored progress to zero even if it previously reported a positive index in the same commitment instance. This contradicts an unconditional per-ID monotonicity interpretation, not this binding's stated association.",
          "limitations": []
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "Notification delivery and consumer behavior are not established by this binding."
          ],
          "target_id": "B_recalculate",
          "aspect": "decomposition",
          "status": "no_issue_found",
          "source_ids": [
            "commitment.go:1:104"
          ],
          "explanation": "The declaration anchor at line 88 and behavior range 88–104 identify recalculate. It returns for an empty voter map, sorts reported indexes, selects position (n-1)/2 and advances only above commitIndex and at or beyond startIndex. For nonempty maps, this position represents strict-majority support for both odd and even voter counts. The association and direct use match the selected calculation responsibility.",
          "alternatives": "A count-based implementation could express the same majority condition. An empty map permits no advance; an unchanged historical commitIndex need not be supported by the replacement map.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "Correct selection of this reported threshold does not establish storage durability or configuration legality. The arithmetic explanation is source inspection, not an executed checker or reachability result.",
          "limitations": []
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "The relation is limited to ordinary leader command commitment and is explicitly insufficient for the complete goal."
          ],
          "target_id": "R_apply_commit",
          "aspect": "decomposition",
          "status": "needs_reading",
          "source_ids": [
            "docs/apply.md:1:100",
            "commitment.go:1:104",
            "api.go:803:907",
            "fsm.go:1:180",
            "raft.go:1440:1584"
          ],
          "explanation": "The direction from G_apply to O_commit is plausible: the documentation describes commitment notification preceding leader FSM dispatch, and commitment.go exposes the notification and index getter. However, the actual leader consumer is absent. The supplied appendEntries implementation shows a follower consuming LeaderCommitIndex, which does not establish the leader handoff. Confirming this dependency requires locating the leader's commit-channel handling and tracing the selected index into processLogs and FSM dispatch.",
          "alternatives": "Followers consume a transmitted leader commit index; batching changes the FSM consumer mechanism. Additional filtering in an unread leader consumer could affect whether every clause of O_commit is necessary for the stated goal.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "O_commit can hold while a consumer dispatches beyond its index or associates completion with the wrong command. Conversely, an additional consumer filter could prevent a calculator error from reaching the goal event. The actual handoff must distinguish these possibilities.",
          "limitations": [
            "The leader-loop consumption, dispatch path and any additional filters remain unread.",
            "The relation's necessity is not fully established by the sequence diagram alone."
          ]
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "This boundary records an unresolved producer responsibility; it does not authorize treating that responsibility as checked or satisfied."
          ],
          "target_id": "R_commit_report_boundary",
          "aspect": "decomposition",
          "status": "no_issue_found",
          "source_ids": [
            "commitment.go:1:104",
            "replication.go:202:298",
            "raft.go:1440:1584",
            "transport.go:1:74"
          ],
          "explanation": "The boundary direction correctly points from the calculator's numeric inputs toward the responsibility for producing meaningful progress. match's comment requires disk agreement through the reported index, while its body checks only membership and increasing numbers. replicateTo calls updateLastAppended after a successful response, and appendEntries stores new entries before success. This supports recording the boundary while leaving the omitted helper and transport/storage guarantees unresolved. The boundary kind does not make report truth a prerequisite for the purely numeric O_commit predicate.",
          "alternatives": "Local writes, ordinary RPC completion, pipelined completion and snapshot catch-up can produce progress through different paths.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "A false increasing report can preserve all local arithmetic properties while causing unsupported commitment. The noted truncation-plus-StoreLogs-failure concern remains contrary evidence for producer soundness; its consequences are not resolved by this boundary review.",
          "limitations": [
            "updateLastAppended is an unresolved callee.",
            "Response correlation, persistence semantics and alternative producers remain unverified."
          ]
        },
        {
          "scope_limitations": [
            "Network schedules, crash durability, elections, configuration-transition safety and end-to-end successful Apply remain excluded.",
            "Arbitrary setter sequences describe component behavior without establishing legal cluster histories."
          ],
          "target_id": "U_commit",
          "aspect": "decomposition",
          "status": "revision_needed",
          "source_ids": [
            "commitment.go:1:104",
            "docs/apply.md:1:100"
          ],
          "explanation": "The four direct code uses coherently cover O_commit, and goal_observable=false correctly prevents a local result from establishing G_apply. However, the audit question asks whether stored progress can decrease across arbitrary voter-map replacements, and its sequence point requires unqualified monotonic progress. That is broader than O_commit's match-report clause. setConfiguration discards removed IDs and initializes newly tracked IDs to zero. Revise these two question strings to distinguish monotonic commitIndex and nondecreasing updates by match from progress reset through removal and readdition.",
          "alternatives": "A separate obligation could investigate preserving historical per-ID progress across membership changes, but its necessity would require additional contract evidence and separate review. The selected O_commit does not assert it.",
          "counterexample_reasoning": "A source-derived, unexecuted sequence is: report index 5 for voter A, remove A, then readd A in the same commitment instance. A's new map entry is zero. No match call decreased stored progress, and commitIndex need not decrease. Treating this as an O_commit violation would misattribute membership reset behavior.",
          "limitations": [
            "The proposed F2 revision requires review before acceptance.",
            "The R_apply_commit handoff remains unresolved.",
            "No executable model, experiment or same-history reachability result was supplied."
          ]
        }
      ],
